  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Smt. Madhur Mathur vs State Of U.P. And Another on 29 July, 2025 High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Neutral Citation No. - 2025:Ahc:125019 Court No. - 75 Case :- Application U/S 528 Bnss No. - 26870 of 2025 Applicant :- Smt. Madhur Mathur Opposite Party :- State of U.P. and Another Counsel for Applicant :- Pawankumar Dubey Counsel for Opposite Party :- G.A. Hon'ble Vikas Budhwar,J. 1.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "Sri Pawan Kumar Dubey, learned counsel for the applicant submits that though the present application under Section 528 of the B.N.S.S. has been filed by the applicant to quash the order of non-bailable-warrants as well as process Under Section 82 of Cr.P.C. & N.S. dated 29.10.2024 passed by Additional Chief Judicial Magistrate-1st, Shahjahanpur in Complaint Case No. 1150 of 2004 (State Vs. Chhotelal and others), Under Section-7(1)/16 (1) and 17 (1) Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954, Police Station G.R.P., District-Shahjahanpur, however non bailable warrants and proceedings under Section 82 of the Cr.P. C. have already been initiated.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Sri Pawan Kumar Dubey, learned counsel for the applicant submits that though the present application under Section 528 of the B.N.S.S. has been filed by the applicant to quash the order of non-bailable-warrants as well as process Under Section 82 of Cr.P.C. & N.S. dated 29.10.2024 passed by Additional Chief Judicial Magistrate-1st, Shahjahanpur in Complaint Case No. 1150 of 2004 (State Vs. Chhotelal and others), Under Section-7(1)/16 (1) and 17 (1) Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954, Police Station G.R.P., District-Shahjahanpur, however non bailable warrants and proceedings under Section 82 of the Cr.P. C. have already been initiated.",
